Beluga modifies only the Java WebRtcAudioTrack output-lifetime/callback path and
adds PlaybackOutputObserver. All unrelated SDK classes and all original native
library payloads are preserved. Source patch, offline builder, input contract
and provenance instructions are in android/webrtc-adapter in the Beluga source.
The derived AAR also contains META-INF/beluga-webrtc-adapter provenance.

The accompanying LICENSE.webrtc and PATENTS.webrtc reproduce the upstream
notices. NOTICE.native.webrtc is the unchanged generated dependency-license
inventory from the exact unprefixed Android build artifact. VERSIONS.webrtc
records that build's source/dependency revisions. The archive's embedded AAR
and all four native payloads match the retained inputs; PROVENANCE.notices.json
records the source URLs, archive identity, member paths and notice hashes.

NOTICE.fork.webrtc separately preserves the pinned source's Shiguredo/Wandbox
attribution. The upstream README identifies Shiguredo patches and LiveKit
changes as Apache-2.0. LICENSE.Apache-2.0 supplies the full license text.

Byte binding establishes provenance, not an independent completeness, legal,
patent, security or runtime clearance. Review of license obligations/security
and delivery of these notices in the built APK remain release requirements.
